# Supabase project credentials — Project Settings > API in the Supabase dashboard.
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your values (.env.local is gitignored).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# services/aiGenerator.ts — Sprint 5 AI Line-Art Assistant. Server-only,
# never exposed to the client. Only the provider(s) you actually call need
# a real value.
FAL_KEY=your-fal-ai-key
OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-key

# Claude (console.anthropic.com → API keys) for the text side of AI: planning
# a book from a description and the editor's command bar. When set, it is
# used instead of OpenAI for those (pictures still come from OpenAI/Fal).
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL defaults to claude-opus-5-5; AI_TEXT_PROVIDER=openai|anthropic forces one.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-anthropic-key
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# AI_TEXT_PROVIDER=anthropic

# Payments (Stripe) — /studio/billing. Leave empty and the app keeps working
# on the Free plan (the billing routes answer "Payments aren't set up yet").
# 1. Stripe dashboard → Products: create "Pro" and "Studio" (recurring, monthly)
#    and two one-off prices for the credit packs; paste the price ids here.
# 2. Developers → Webhooks → add endpoint https://<your-site>/api/billing/webhook
#    with events checkout.session.completed and customer.subscription.created /
#    .updated / .deleted; paste its signing secret as STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET.
# 3. Settings → Billing → Customer portal: turn it on (plan changes, cancel).
# Labels shown on the page live in src/lib/plans.ts — keep them in step.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
STRIPE_PRICE_PRO=price_...
STRIPE_PRICE_STUDIO=price_...
STRIPE_PRICE_CREDITS_100=price_...
STRIPE_PRICE_CREDITS_500=price_...
# Supabase → Project Settings → API → service_role. Server only: the webhook
# uses it to record plans and bought credits. Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
# Public address of the site, for Stripe's return links (defaults to the request's origin).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-site.example
